### ==========================================================================
### NexaChat live-demo requests (REST client script)
### Works in JetBrains HTTP Client (IDEA/WebStorm/PhpStorm) and VS Code
### REST Client. Run top-to-bottom against a local backend:
###   docker compose up -d && psql ... < demo/seed.sql   # provides +84900000002
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080   |   Prefix: /api/v1   |   Auth: JWT Bearer
### ==========================================================================

### 1. Register the demo account -------------------------------------------
### TOLERANT: a 409 PHONE_EXISTS simply means the account already exists
### (the demo was run before) — ignore it and go straight to step 2 (login).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+84900000010",
  "password": "password123",
  "displayName": "Demo"
}

### 2. Login — captures accessToken and refreshToken as client variables ----
### {{token}} is reused by every authenticated request below.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+84900000010",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 3. List my contacts -----------------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Open the direct conversation with Binh (+84900000002) ----------------
### Idempotent: 201 when created, 200 when it already existed. Either way the
### conversation id is saved as {{conversationId}}.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/conversations/direct
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+84900000002"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.id);
%}

### 5. Inbox ----------------------------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Send a TEXT message (REST fallback for the WebSocket path) -----------
### Fixed clientMessageId: replaying the request is idempotent (200 + same row).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4e6f-8b7c-1d2e3f4a5b6c",
  "type": "TEXT",
  "content": "Hello from REST"
}

### 7. Message history — newest first, page size 5 --------------------------
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Mark conversation as read up to seq 1 --------------------------------
### Watermark is monotonic; any non-negative seq is accepted (204).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/conversations/{{conversationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "upToSeq": 1
}

### 9. Refresh the token pair ----------------------------------------------
### Public endpoint (no Authorization header needed): refreshToken is
### single-use and rotates — the new pair is stored back into the variables.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 10. File upload/download -----------------------------------------------
### Create the fixture first (repo root): a tiny valid PDF. Plain text has NO
### magic signature, so hello.txt would be rejected 415 by the byte sniff.
###   printf '%%PDF-1.4\n%%%%EOF\n' > demo/fixtures/hello.pdf
### (or drop any small PDF/PNG there under that name).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hello.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./demo/fixtures/hello.pdf
--WebAppBoundary--

> {%
    client.global.set("attId", response.body.id);
%}

### 11. Send a FILE message that references the uploaded attachment ----------
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "5c1f9a2e-7b3d-4c8a-9e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f",
  "type": "FILE",
  "content": "hello.pdf",
  "attachmentIds": ["{{attId}}"]
}

### 12. Download the attachment bytes --------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/attachments/{{attId}}/content
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error demos ------------------------------------------------------------
### Uploading a file larger than 25MB  -> 413 FILE_TOO_LARGE
### Uploading wrong magic bytes        -> 415 MIME_NOT_ALLOWED
### (an .exe renamed .png, or plain-text hello.txt)
